  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "This problem has subtasks.\n\nYou are given two integers LLL and RRR (L≤RL \\leq RL≤R).\n\nYou want to purify each integer in this range. To purify an integer xxx between LLL and RRR, you must pay a cost, which is computed as follows:\n\n\nChoose a positive integer kkk and some integers a1,a2,…,aka_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_ka1​,a2​,…,ak​ such that:\n\nL≤ai≤RL \\leq a_i \\leq RL≤ai​≤R for each iii.\nlcm(a1,a2,…,ak)=x\\text{lcm}(a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_k) = xlcm(a1​,a2​,…,ak​)=x\n\n\nThe cost of purifying xxx using these integers equals max⁡(a1,a2,…,ak)\\max(a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_k)max(a1​,a2​,…,ak​).\nFor example, if L=12L = 12L=12 and R=74R = 74R=74, to purify x=60x = 60x=60,\n\n\nYou can choose the sequence (20,30,20,60)(20, 30, 20, 60)(20,30,20,60) with cost 606060; or\nYou can choose the sequence (20,30)(20, 30)(20,30) with cost 303030; or\nYou can choose the sequence (12,20)(12, 20)(12,20) with cost 202020.\nHowever, you cannot choose the sequence (3,4,5,12)(3, 4, 5, 12)(3,4,5,12), because even though its lcm equals 606060, it uses integers &lt;L\\lt L&lt;L.\nFind the minimum cost to purify every integer from LLL to RRR (inclusive of LLL and RRR).\n\nYou must answer TTT independent test cases.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of a single line, containing two space-separated integers LLL and RRR.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the minimum cost to purify all numbers from LLL to RRR (inclusive of LLL and RRR).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤3⋅1051 \\leq T \\leq 3\\cdot 10^51≤T≤3⋅105",
      "1≤L≤R≤3⋅1051 \\leq L \\leq R \\leq 3\\cdot 10^51≤L≤R≤3⋅105",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask 111 (202020 points):** L=1L = 1L=1 for all tests.",
      "**Subtask 222 (808080 points):** No further constraints."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
