        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n2 6\n3 12\n1 1000",
        "output": "17\n67\n149564",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: With L=2L = 2L=2 and R=6R = 6R=6,\n\nThe cost of purifying 222 will be 222, by choosing the sequence (2)(2)(2).\nThe cost of purifying 333 will be 333, by choosing the sequence (3)(3)(3).\nThe cost of purifying 444 will be 444, by choosing the sequence (2,4)(2, 4)(2,4).\nThe cost of purifying 555 will be 555, by choosing the sequence (5)(5)(5).\nThe cost of purifying 666 will be 333, by choosing the sequence (2,3)(2, 3)(2,3).\n\nThe total cost of purification will be 2+3+4+5+3=172+3+4+5+3=172+3+4+5+3=17\nTest case 222: The costs of purifying the numbers from 333 to 121212 are: [3,4,5,6,7,8,9,10,11,4][3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 4][3,4,5,6,7,8,9,10,11,4]. Their sum is 676767."
      }
